--TEST--
`Sheet::cell` and `Sheet::column` on a finished sheet throw a message that names the sheet and says it is finished, after the next sheet starts and after the workbook is finished: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-roster
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Sheet::cell
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Sheet::column
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook;

var $book = Workbook::createInMemory();
var $orders = $book->sheet("Orders");
$orders->add(["order" => 1042, "qty" => 3]);
echo $orders->cell("qty", 2), "\n";

// Starting the next sheet finishes this one.
var $returns = $book->sheet("Returns");
try {
    $orders->cell("qty", 2);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $orders->column("qty");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

$returns->add(["order" => 1042]);
$book->finish();
try {
    $returns->cell("order", 2);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
B2
The sheet `Orders` is finished, so `cell` and `column` cannot return its addresses. A sheet is finished when the workbook starts the next sheet.
The sheet `Orders` is finished, so `cell` and `column` cannot return its addresses. A sheet is finished when the workbook starts the next sheet.
The sheet `Returns` is finished, because the workbook is finished. `finish` is the last call on a workbook.
